# PRIVATE DATA - never publish.
# A configuration is a list of what is in somebody's living room, and donor dumps
# belong to other people. The tool reads these off your own remote; none of them
# need to be in the repository.
# (No trailing comments on pattern lines: git treats them as part of the path.)
# Written by the bundle workflow so a frozen build can name itself. Generated, never
# committed - a stale one would make every build claim the wrong version.
src/afterglow/_build.py

*.ezhex
*.EzHex
*.EZHex
*.EZHEX
*_extracted/
configs/
channel_logos/

# Private device libraries and captures. The application writes its live library under
# XDG_DATA_HOME, but these legacy in-tree paths must stay ignored during migration.
/src/afterglow/library/devices/
/src/afterglow/library/captures/
/src/afterglow/library/ir-captures/
/library/devices/
/library/captures/
/library/ir-captures/
/test_external_archive.json
/local-library/
/user-library/

# Project files describe a real home, and carry the MAC of any paired RF base.
#
# Deny by default at the repository root. The list below used to be the whole rule, and
# it is a list of names someone thought of after the fact - a project file has reached a
# commit twice because its name matched no pattern that existed yet. Every private
# artifact this project produces is written to the working directory: project.json,
# project_actual_mce.json, home_logi_dump.json, test_external_archive.json. Nothing
# legitimate is: all 34 tracked .json files live under src/afterglow/library/, and a
# leading slash confines this to the root, so they are untouched.
#
# Adding a genuinely shareable .json at the root therefore needs `git add -f` and a
# moment's thought about what is in it. That is the point.
/*.json

# Kept as well, because these names are also dangerous in a subdirectory.
project.json
project_*.json
*_project.json
*_proj.json
*_dump.json

# PROPRIETARY - Logitech's, not ours. Redistributing any of this is not ok.
# Firmware images and anything recovered by decompiling them.
*.hfw
lua_src/
ffdec_out/

# Build / scratch
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*_work/
